# The Recommended rule of the same name holds every other hedge.
# `relatively` sits here, because it sometimes states a real
# comparison (`relatively few nodes run the agent, compared with the
# fleet`). Most hits give no baseline (`a relatively small number of
# objects`), so the fix gives the number or the baseline. `potentially`
# stays out, because the redundant-pair rule reports `could
# potentially`.
#
# `effectively`, `virtually`, and `practically` each read two ways.
# `the flag effectively disables the cache` can mean that the flag
# disables it in effect but not in name, or that it disables it well.
# `practically` means `almost` or `in practice`. The three sit here,
# because the plain sense is sometimes the one meant (`use the cache
# effectively`). They hit 14 paragraphs in the kubernetes and nix.dev
# docs.
expr main [relatively, effectively, virtually, practically]
let message "Hedge. State the claim or drop it."
let description "Flags relatively, effectively, virtually, and practically, which soften a claim or read two ways."
let becomes ""
let kind "Style"
allows "Few nodes run the agent."
allows "The flag disables the cache."
